      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wauseon%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1869, Wauseon outpaced Fulton County's original seat Ottokee and was named the county seat after railroad success.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wauseon%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Andrew Carnegie funded Wauseon Public Library in 1906, giving the town a classic Carnegie library building.",
